fOrganizer","owner":"dj0894","html_url":"https://github.com/dj0894/KitchenShelfOrganizer","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Swift","description":"KitchenShelfOrganizer is an IOS app helping users to organise kitchen shelf efficiently at the home. Proper management and proactive notification will result in efficient Kitchen management and reducing waste.","topics":[],"score":248344,"global_rank":65257},{"name":"jardiamj/CSC143_Utility","owner":"jardiamj","html_url":"https://github.com/jardiamj/CSC143_Utility","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Shell","description":"Utility tools for CSC143 class - Java II","topics":[],"score":248340,"global_rank":65258},{"name":"Eugeneberezin/project7-iExpense","owner":"Eugeneberezin","html_url":"https://github.com/Eugeneberezin/project7-iExpense","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Swift","description":"Our next two projects are going to start pushing your SwiftUI skills beyond the basics, as we explore apps that have multiple screens, that load and save user data, and have more complex user interfaces.  In this project we\u2019re going to build iExpense, which is an expense tracker that separates personal costs from business costs. At its core this is an app with a form (how much did you spend?) and a list (here are the amounts you spent), but in order to accomplish those two things you\u2019re going to need to learn how to:  Present and dismiss a second screen of data. Delete rows from a list Save and load user data \u2026and more.  There\u2019s lots to do, so let\u2019s get started: create a new iOS app using the Single View App template, naming it \u201ciExpense\u201d. We\u2019ll be using that for the main project, but first lets take a closer look at the new techniques required for this project\u2026","topics":[],"score":248340,"global_rank":65261},{"name":"CarterKekoa/HaskellRecursionAndPattern","owner":"CarterKekoa","html_url":"https://github.com/CarterKekoa/Haske